The RFP and selection processes will be governed by RCUH policies and procedures applicable to federally funded projects, which includes a specific section for Procurement and Disbursing.

Under the Procurement and Disbursing Section, 2.001, it is stated that the intent of the procurement policies and procedures is “to reflect an environment that provides Projects with the best possible solution for obtaining goods and service in a timely and cost effective manner, while ensuring compliance with applicable regulations and promoting good business practices. The purchases of goods and services through the RCUH will be conducted to promote open and free competition. Adherence to competitive procurement practices shall be carried out based on the following general principles:

• Obtaining best value;

• Ensuring compliance with all applicable laws, regulations, and RCUH policies and procedures;

• Promoting good business practices;

• Engaging in fair and ethical business relationships;

• Providing transparency and accountability;

